---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/layout/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import AlertBox from '../components/ui/AlertBox.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Professional Review Status" description="Current status of independent professional review at Standby Generator Guide and the information we will disclose if article-specific review is completed.">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ href: '/', label: 'Home' }, { label: 'Professional Review Status' }]} />
    <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-bold text-primary">Professional review: current status</h1>
    <div class="mt-6">
      <AlertBox type="info" title="No independent professional reviews completed">No licensed professional has reviewed our articles. Source citations and editorial research are not a substitute for independent, article-specific technical review. We do not claim a reviewer, credential, signoff, or endorsement that we cannot document.</AlertBox>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-hgg mt-6">
      <h2>How to read our current attribution</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Topic-specific editorial desks perform desk research; these organizational bylines are not individual people, trade licenses, or professional qualifications.</li>
        <li>Sources listed on an article identify where information came from. A manufacturer page is not an independent test or endorsement.</li>
        <li>Checking a document or safety source does not mean a licensed professional reviewed the article.</li>
        <li>Use exact model manuals, qualified local professionals, and the authority having jurisdiction for decisions about a property.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>How a qualified professional can review future articles</h2>
<p>We maintain a written review brief for priority topics: generator sizing, fuel capacity, electrical and gas boundaries, placement, transfer equipment, safety and exact-model comparisons. Each review must identify the person, relevant competence, licensing jurisdiction where applicable, source version, scope, conflicts and date. A review becomes public only after an actual review record and permission are documented.</p>
<p><strong>Current status:</strong> no independent US professional has signed off on any article. Pages must continue showing that status until a documented review exists. A manufacturer manual check, employee research-desk byline or automated test does not count as licensed review.</p>
<p>Have relevant, verifiable credentials and want to discuss reviewing content? Use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. This is an invitation to discuss a potential future review, not a promise of employment, compensation or publication.</p>
<h2>Disclosure if article review is completed</h2>
      <p>If an article later receives professional review, its page will identify the reviewer, the credential and licensing jurisdiction where applicable, the review date, the article-specific scope, and any relevant affiliation or compensation. A review will be attributed only to the article and scope actually reviewed.</p>
      <h2>What a professional review does—and does not—establish</h2>
<p>Desk research checks published evidence. Professional review evaluates a named article and defined technical scope against a documented content version. Neither is a site inspection, permit approval, generator performance test or guarantee of suitability for your home.</p>
<p>A future review record must include profession, license type and jurisdiction, a public verification link, employer or affiliations, compensation, conflicts, reviewed version and limitations. We publish a license number or supplied headshot only with permission. Material edits require renewed review; a withdrawn or superseded record cannot support an active review badge.</p>
<h2>Corrections and questions</h2>
      <p>Research dates, source links, and professional-review status are separate records. For factual corrections, <a href="/contact/">send us the page URL and a supporting source</a>; see the <a href="/corrections-policy/">corrections policy</a> for details.</p>
      <p>Read the <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a> for source standards, independence, and current limitations.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
